S3  why this is not a spherical estimate: linear superposition of single-mass phantoms
    two single-mass phantoms added at the saddle: C = 2*(1/(4 pi (1/2)^2)) = 2/pi = +0.6366
    the nonlinear solve gives C(0.02) = -0.6450; sign and size both differ
K5 PASS C_super=+0.6366 > 0.5 (the superposition has the WRONG SIGN)

